//   https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/FAA-H-8083-28B.pdf
//   (ch 4 standard atmosphere; ch 11 fronts; ch 12 lapse rates and the LCL; ch 13 stability; ch 16 mountain wave, lenticulars, rotor;
//    ch 18 fog types; ch 20 icing; ch 22 thunderstorm life cycle, microbursts, avoidance; ch 24 METAR body, remarks, AO2, SLP, T group, PIREP format;
//    ch 26 SIGMET, Convective SIGMET, AIRMET Sierra/Tango/Zulu and CONUS graphical AIRMETs; ch 27 FB winds aloft, TAF FM/TEMPO/PROB30, Low-Level SIGWX prog)
// AC 00-45H Change 2, Aviation Weather Services, shown as CANCELLED, consolidated into the Aviation Weather Handbook:
//   https://www.faa.gov/regulations_policies/advisory_circulars/index.cfm/go/document.information/documentID/1030235
// AviationWeather.gov data help (METAR, TAF, G-AIRMET, SIGMET, Convective SIGMET, PIREP, FB product notes): https://aviationweather.gov/help/data/
// Private Pilot Airplane ACS, FAA-S-ACS-6C, task PA.I.C Weather Information: https://www.faa.gov/training_testing/testing/acs/private_airplane_acs_6.pdf
// Pilot's Handbook of Aeronautical Knowledge, FAA-H-8083-25C, chapters 12 (weather theory: cloud base by 4.4°F convergence, dew and frost, fog, stability,
